{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: the original model put the prior sampling statement on transformed parameter `beta`, which SafeStan does not allow. The rewritten model places the equivalent built-in multivariate normal prior on the top-level parameter `beta_tilde`. Since `beta = R_inv * beta_tilde`, the induced covariance for `beta_tilde` is `100 * R * R'`, computed deterministically from context data in transformed data as `beta_tilde_cov`. The protected-data likelihood `y ~ normal(Q * beta_tilde + alpha, sigma)` is unchanged, and no data fields were added.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=1> N;
  int<lower=1> M;
  matrix[M, N] X;
  vector[N] y;
}

transformed data {
  // Compute, thin, and then scale QR decomposition
  matrix[N, M] Q = qr_Q(X')[, 1:M] * N;
  matrix[M, M] R = qr_R(X')[1:M, ] / N;
  matrix[M, M] R_inv = inverse(R);
  matrix[M, M] beta_tilde_cov = 100 * R * R';
}

parameters {
  vector[M] beta_tilde;
  real alpha;
  real<lower=0> sigma;
}

transformed parameters {
  vector[M] beta = R_inv * beta_tilde;
}

model {
  beta_tilde ~ multi_normal(rep_vector(0, M), beta_tilde_cov);
  alpha ~ normal(0, 10);
  sigma ~ cauchy(0, 10);

  y ~ normal(Q * beta_tilde + alpha, sigma);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"M":1,"N":5,"X":[[4.203632243761758,4.068335508049714,6.094982411785829,5.134059952157438,4.345512643674157]],"y":[5.0,3.0,5.0,3.0,5.0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
